<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Stretches of sine and cosine waves</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The graph of \(y = {@fname@}\,x\) is mapped onto \(y = {@wdisp@}\) by two stretches.</p><div>(a) The stretch with the \(x\)-axis invariant has stretch factor [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><div>(b) The stretch with the \(y\)-axis invariant has stretch factor [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><div>(c) The point \({@Pd@}\) on \(y = {@fname@}\,x\) is mapped to ( [[input:ans3]] \(^\circ\) , [[input:ans4]] ) [[validation:ans3]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Every point moves away from the invariant axis by the same factor.</p><p>(a) Multiplying by \({@dnum(a)@}\) outside the function multiplies every \(y\)-coordinate by \({@dnum(a)@}\): a stretch with the \(x\)-axis invariant, stretch factor \({@a@}\).</p><p>(b) Replacing \(x\) by \({@b@}x\) makes the wave repeat \({@b@}\) times as often, so every \(x\)-coordinate is multiplied by \({@sx@}\): a stretch with the \(y\)-axis invariant, stretch factor \({@sx@}\).</p><p>(c) \({@Pd@} \mapsto \left({@px@}^\circ \times {@sx@},\ {@py@} \times {@a@}\right) = \left({@ix3@}^\circ, {@iy3@}\right)\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[hits(L,s,tol) := length(sublist(L, lambda([v], is(abs(v-s) <= tol))));
matchset(L,S,tol) := is(length(L) = length(S)) and every(lambda([s], is(hits(L,s,tol) = 1)), S);
allgenuine(L,S,tol) := every(lambda([v], some(lambda([s], is(abs(v-s) <= tol)), S)), L);
validate_angles(ex) := if (setp(ex) or listp(ex)) and every(lambda([v], numberp(ev(v,simp))), if setp(ex) then listify(ex) else ex) then "" else "Type the angles as numbers inside curly brackets, separated by commas, for example {30, 150}. Do not type the degree sign.";
r1(v) := float(floor(10*v+1/2)/10);
ang1(v) := block([r], r: floor(10*v+1/2), if integerp(r/10) then string(r/10) else string(float(r/10)));
setraw(L) := if L = [] then "\\{\\,\\}" else sconcat("\\{", simplode(map(lambda([v], sconcat(ang1(v), "^\\circ")), sort(L)), ", "), "\\}");
degraw(v) := sconcat(ang1(v), "^\\circ");
setstr(L) := sconcat("\\(", setraw(L), "\\)");
angc(v) := block([al], al: float(acos(v)*180/%pi), if abs(al) < 1e-9 then [0,360] elseif abs(al-180) < 1e-9 then [180] else [al, 360-al]);
angs(v) := block([al], al: float(asin(v)*180/%pi), if abs(al) < 1e-9 then [0,180,360] elseif abs(al-90) < 1e-9 then [90] elseif abs(al+90) < 1e-9 then [270] elseif al > 0 then [al, 180-al] else [180-al, 360+al]);
qroots(A,B,C) := if A = 0 then (if B = 0 then [] else [-C/B]) elseif B^2-4*A*C < 0 then [] else [(-B-sqrt(B^2-4*A*C))/(2*A), (-B+sqrt(B^2-4*A*C))/(2*A)];
inrange(L) := sublist(L, lambda([v], is(abs(float(v)) <= 1+1e-12)));
uniqf(L) := unique(map(lambda([v], float(floor(10000*v+1/2)/10000)), L));
nice(v) := block([r], r: floor(1000*v+1/2)/1000, if integerp(r) then r else float(r));
res2(v) := block([r], r: floor(100*v+1/2)/100, if integerp(r) then string(r) else string(float(r)));
tm(n, s) := if n = 0 then "" elseif n = 1 then sconcat(" + ", s) elseif n = -1 then sconcat(" - ", s) elseif n > 0 then sconcat(" + ", string(n), s) else sconcat(" - ", string(-n), s);
tc(n) := if n = 0 then "" elseif n > 0 then sconcat(" + ", string(n)) else sconcat(" - ", string(-n));
lead(n, s) := if n = 1 then s elseif n = -1 then sconcat("-", s) else sconcat(string(n), s);
/* Design: stretches of sine and cosine waves (stretch factors a and 1/b), with the image of a point. a and b are never 1. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 2, Chapter 7, Section B, B5 and the key points. */
L: [[1,3,5],[0,2,3],[1,1/2,4],[0,4,1/2],[1,2,1/3],[0,3/2,2],[1,5,3],[0,3,2/3],[1,4,3/2],[0,1/2,6]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
fs: L[ix][1]; a: L[ix][2]; b: L[ix][3];
fname: if fs = 1 then "\\sin" else "\\cos";
dnum(v) := if integerp(v) then string(v) else string(float(v));
bxs(b) := if b = 1 then " x" elseif integerp(b) then sconcat(" ", string(b), "x") elseif num(b) = 1 then sconcat("\\tfrac{x}{", string(denom(b)), "}") else sconcat("\\tfrac{", string(num(b)), "x}{", string(denom(b)), "}");
wdisp: sconcat(dnum(a), fname, bxs(b));
px: if fs = 1 then 90 else 180; py: if fs = 1 then 1 else -1;
sy: a; sx: 1/b; ix3: px/b; iy3: py*a;
ra: 1/a; xb: b; ixb: px*b;
Pd: sconcat("(", string(px), "^\\circ, ", string(py), ")");
sy4: float(sy)+0.004; sx4: float(sx)+0.004;
]]></text>
